        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, sacbH2 (0.08 g, 0.30 mmol) and NEt3 (42 μL, 0.30 mmol) were dissolved in MeOH/MeCN (15 mL, 2:1 v/v). Solid Cu(acac)2 (0.03 g, 0.10 mmol) and Dy(acac)3·2H2O (0.10 g, 0.20 mmol) were added together. The light-green suspension was stirred for 30 min until the solids dissolved, filtered, and left to evaporate slowly at room temperature. After 3 days, light-yellow needle-like crystals were collected, washed with cold MeOH (2 × 2 mL) and Et2O (2 × 5 mL), and dried in air. Yield 52% based on the organic chelate. The crystal structure contains four MeCN and two MeOH lattice solvent molecules.",
