        "summary": "dc χMT at 0.1 T falls from 56.20 cm3 K mol−1 at 300 K to 46.44 cm3 K mol−1 at 10 K, then rises to 48.88 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K, indicating low-temperature ferromagnetic exchange together with Dy(III) anisotropy. Magnetization at 7 T is about 24.8 NμB and does not saturate. No zero-field ac out-of-phase signal is observed; under 1100 Oe only low-temperature χM'' tails appear, consistent with fast relaxation and residual QTM rather than an efficient SMM.",
